  "synthesis_conclusions": [
    "Only a small proportion of available studies on sound and human performance can be used to inform room acoustic design decisions, and their generalizability is limited to settings similar to experimental conditions (source type, sound-task interaction, room type, task type, personal factors).",
    "Distinguishing between the effect of sound on human performance and the effect of room acoustics on the sound environment is crucial to avoid over-estimating the role of room acoustics.",
    "Evidence regarding the effectiveness of strategies to control the sound environment through room acoustic design is currently lacking and should be a future research focus.",
    "Little knowledge is available on the effect of room acoustics on job performance across various workplaces and job types, highlighting the complexity of measurement in these contexts."
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "Lack of evidence on the effectiveness of room acoustic design strategies to control the sound environment for human task performance.",
    "Limited generalizability of existing studies due to specific experimental settings (source type, sound-task interaction, room type, task type, personal factors).",
    "Need for research on a broader variety of space typologies beyond open-plan offices, classrooms, and laboratory booths.",
    "Future studies should investigate and include the role of the sound environment for specific tasks or jobs, rather than just isolated abilities.",
    "Need to operationalize the full process of complex tasks, including planning, prioritizing, and executing, not just individual task performance.",
    "Future studies should address older age groups and a wider range of personal factors beyond noise sensitivity and working memory capacity.",
    "Need for studies where auditory conditions are congruent with other sensory conditions (e.g., visual setting) in natural working environments.",
    "Investigation of the visibility of sound sources and its impact on performance decrement."
  ],
